>>
Rule 1 (features must have an allowed dtype for Relu)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 2 (exclude unsupported dtypes: bool and complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (tensor dimensions are non-negative; empty dimensions allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (operation name must be a valid string from the allowed set)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "relu" ∨ v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "linear" ∨ v_1 = "sum"
>>
Rule 5 (for unsigned integer inputs, all values are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (piecewise dtype guard mirroring allowed integer and float ranges)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 then true else if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then true else false
